  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 129 PM MDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nSlightly cooler, but still above seasonal temperatures remain in the offing\nfrom Thursday into Saturday, as upper level ridging rebuilds across the \nRockies ahead of stout upper trough digging across the Pacific Northwest. \nThere will be enough residual moisture to support more isolated afternoon\nshowers over the higher terrain through this period. \n\nBy Sunday, models indicate said Pac Northwest system digging into the Great \nBasin, with increasing southwest flow aloft leading to breezy to possibly \nwindy conditions over and near the higher terrain. This normally would\nindicate potential fire weather concerns, however, latest fuels updates\nare coming in non-critical at this time. Increasing moisture within the\nincreasing flow aloft brings increasing chances of precipitation to areas\nover and near the Continental Divide later Sunday into Monday, with strong\nwest to southwest flow continuing across the Rockies Tuesday and possibly into \nWednesday, as the system translates into the Central High Plains. This would \nspread precipitation chances and cooler temperatures across south central and \nsoutheast Colorado Monday night and Tuesday, with the potential for severe \nweather across the far southeast plains Tuesday, dependent on the movement\nof secondary energy digging down the back side of the system. While model\ndifferences remain on timing and location of this stronger system, cooler\nand more unsettled weather remains in the offing across south central and \nsoutheast Colorado for early next week.",
